WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:22.361 --> 00:00:24.861
(blues music)

00:00:39.961 --> 00:00:41.336
- The cool thing about
Bilbo Walker is that

00:00:41.336 --> 00:00:44.679
he grew up in the same Mississippi
Delta blues environment

00:00:44.679 --> 00:00:47.778
as like Charley Patton, Robert
Johnson, or Muddy Waters,

00:00:47.778 --> 00:00:49.639
or Howlin' Wolf or B.B. King.

00:00:49.639 --> 00:00:52.108
And when he performs, it feels like that.

00:00:52.108 --> 00:00:54.358
It is like a living fossil.

00:01:09.171 --> 00:01:10.658
He's out there in the boonies,

00:01:10.658 --> 00:01:13.378
not even a town, it's just out in a field.

00:01:13.378 --> 00:01:17.199
And I also love the fact that
it's just so hard to find

00:01:17.199 --> 00:01:19.282
right until you're at it.

00:01:29.407 --> 00:01:32.166
It's an old army barracks,
Quonset hut cut in pieces,

00:01:32.166 --> 00:01:34.447
moved onto this property himself.

00:01:34.447 --> 00:01:37.437
Real authentic juke joint is
gonna be African-American owned

00:01:37.437 --> 00:01:39.136
because it comes out of that culture

00:01:39.136 --> 00:01:43.303
and it's probably gonna have
a big personality behind it.

00:02:15.738 --> 00:02:19.287
Real juke joints that are
still operating with live music

00:02:19.287 --> 00:02:22.037
I can probably count on one hand.

00:02:23.887 --> 00:02:26.327
I used to say, “You're not gonna get

00:02:26.327 --> 00:02:27.767
anymore juke joints like that.”

00:02:27.767 --> 00:02:30.308
I would have to say Bilbo's
just gets grandfathered in.

00:02:30.308 --> 00:02:31.879
It's just such a real thing

00:02:31.879 --> 00:02:34.047
and it's kind of an extension of him

00:02:34.047 --> 00:02:38.130
and sort of what he's
been doing his whole life.

